                <pb facs="0607" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13329/1–3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador O’Brien.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Root instructs Mr. O’Brien to convey appropriate expressions of the
                    President’s and Government’s sympathy with the Japanese Government in the
                    terrible disaster resulting from the explosion on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Matsushima.</hi></p>
            </div>
